{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/pulls/793","id":4976682042,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTatV2s8AAAABKKIkOg","html_url":"https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/pull/793","diff_url":"https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/pull/793.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/pull/793.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/issues/793","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/pulls/793/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/pulls/793/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/issues/793/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/statuses/bb496b533a49c4c06c58d11319e11c2eca793ad5","number":793,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Retain encrypted focused development preparation failures","user":{"login":"Kgray44","id":64373011,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64373011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44","html_url":"https://github.com/Kgray44","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Preparation failures currently skip the browser-execution uploader, leaving no encrypted setup/build evidence. This change adds a separate trusted preparation capture and publication route with creation-bound producer cleanup, bounded private streams, the accepted encryption identity, exact durable file checks and an independent output nonce. The uploader can retain the genuine encrypted preparation pair after failure; the original preparation result remains a failure.\n\nThe original development run [39881765636/1](https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/actions/runs/39881765636) remains failed with zero artifacts; its underlying preparation cause remains unknown and its unpublished files cannot be recovered. Browser-execution labels and publication, consumer contracts and finite authority remain unchanged.\n\nThe preserved first candidate 53383782701d1717e8bc73462d2eae3298210215 failed [normal qualification 39887104918/1](https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/actions/runs/39887104918) after historical fixture approvals expired. The follow-up changes only test clocks: per-case recorded approval/floor times, synchronous predecessor binding with exact Date restoration, and a file-URL preload for direct-execution fixture children. Production expiry checks and every original guard assertion, 20-second child timeout and 120-Git-operation bound remain intact. New assertions retain expiry denial and prove clock restoration on success and validation failure.\n\nValidation:\n- Preparation fixtures: 18 cases,13 passed locally and 5 explicitly Linux-only; these need normal hosted Linux qualification.\n- Corrected historical-clock selection: 17 admission assertions passed before the combined 240-second local outer limit; exception-file completion was not proved. Cleanup passed in 212 ms. This run remains incomplete.\n- Accepted-main comparison reproduced the R25 predecessor import failure. Two missing-fixture attempts and a 180-second bounded comparison remain preserved; the other five exception failures are established by the first protected run, not claimed as locally baseline-reproduced.\n- The prior browser compatibility selection has 30 Windows/POSIX failures matched on accepted main with identical transitive sources; it is not Linux proof.\n- Documentation index/validation, feature synchronization/validation and formatting pass. No feature catalog change is required.\n\nIndependent exact-source review and a new normal protected Mainline Decision are required for the corrected candidate. Installation requires protected landing and independent verification of the landed tree. No consumer rerun is authorized by this infrastructure repair.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-23T01:59:20Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T03:11:38Z","closed_at":"2026-10-23T03:11:36Z","merged_at":"2026-10-23T03:11:36Z","merge_commit_sha":"b2d901af5646ce76b3b2bd5a88e1ad8563c2db57","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Kgray44:codex/development-preparation-retention-20261022","ref":"codex/development-preparation-retention-20261022","repo":{"id":1303074266,"node_id":"R_kgDOTatV2g","name":"treasurehuntSoT","full_name":"Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT","owner":{"login":"Kgray44","id":64373011,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64373011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44","html_url":"https://github.com/Kgray44","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/e